"Kent Paul Dolan" <xanthian@well.com> writes:
> This is too simple, of course, because the monster
> mix is situational.

I wonder if a reasonable approximation to the monster mix for this
purpose could be found by analysing the vanquished lists from
ascension dumps? The relevant assumptions being:

a) we're only worried about monsters we plan to fight; ones we go
around, leave alone, or never meet, we don't care too much what our
weapon _would_ have done to them.

b) in nearly every case, any monster you fight, you kill.

c) third-party kills are negligble.

(Ascension dumps rather than generic dumps, to ensure that all parts
of the game get a fair representation; Gnomebane would be great for
the Mines, but is hardly a long-term proposition.)

